                <!-- Assumptions Tab -->
                <div id="subtab-cheatsheet-assumptions" class="sub-tab-panel" style="display: none;">
                    <div class="cheatsheet-container">
                        <h1 class="cheatsheet-title">⚠️ Technical Assumptions and Storage Requirements</h1>
                        
                        <div class="assumption-box">
                            <h4 class="assumption-title">Configuration ID Storage</h4>
                            <p class="assumption-description">
                                The <span class="assumption-code">configurationId</span> must be stored in the Salesforce Quote object field <span class="assumption-code">SBQQ__Quote__c.SAP_VCP_Config_ID__c</span>.
                                This ID is required to retrieve, update, or delete configurations via SAP VC APIs.<br/><br/>
                                The End-to-End tab saves this value automatically after Create Configuration via the Apex method <span class="assumption-code">saveConfigIdToQuote</span>.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="assumption-box">
                            <h4 class="assumption-title">Pricing Document ID Storage - Time-To-Live ¿?</h4>
                            <p class="assumption-description">
                                The <span class="assumption-code">documentId</span> (UUID format) must be stored after creating a pricing document.
                                <br/><br/>
                                <strong>⚠️ CRITICAL:</strong> Pricing documents in SAP have a Time-To-Live (TTL) and will expire/be deleted after a period of inactivity.
                                If you receive error <span class="assumption-code">404 - documentId not found</span>, the document has expired and you must create a new one.
                                <br/><br/>
                                <strong>Recommendation:</strong> Store in <span class="assumption-code">SBQQ__Quote__c.SAP_Pricing_Doc_ID__c</span> and track creation timestamp to detect expiration.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="assumption-box">
                            <h4 class="assumption-title">ETag Storage for Configuration Updates</h4>
                            <p class="assumption-description">
                                The <span class="assumption-code">ETag</span> header from the configuration creation response must be stored in the database.
                                The GET configuration endpoint does NOT return the ETag in the response body or headers.
                                When updating a configuration (PATCH), the <span class="assumption-code">If-Match</span> header with the stored ETag value is required.
                                <br/><br/>
                                <strong>Recommendation:</strong> Store in <span class="assumption-code">SBQQ__Quote__c.SAP_Config_ETag__c</span> (Text field, 255 chars).
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="assumption-box">
                            <h4 class="assumption-title">If-Match Header for Pricing Operations</h4>
                            <p class="assumption-description">
                                Creating items, conditions, or updating pricing documents requires the <span class="assumption-code">If-Match</span> header.
                                This value is obtained from the <span class="assumption-code">ETag</span> response header of the preceding operation:
                                <br/><br/>
                                • <strong>Create Document</strong> → returns ETag (e.g., <span class="assumption-code">W/"1"</span>)<br/>
                                • <strong>Create Items</strong> → requires If-Match from previous step, returns new ETag<br/>
                                • <strong>Add Conditions</strong> → requires If-Match from previous step, returns new ETag<br/>
                                <br/>
                                <strong>Recommendation:</strong> Store the latest ETag in <span class="assumption-code">SBQQ__Quote__c.SAP_Pricing_ETag__c</span> and update it after each successful operation.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
